    "created_at": "2026-11-12T12:13:05Z",
    "updated_at": "2026-11-12T12:13:56Z",
    "body": "The problem is that the escaping happens when calling `pi.setAttribute('x', 'y\\rz')` or something else that trigger changes PI attributes and calls https://dom.spec.whatwg.org/#update-data-from-attributes.\n\nBut when serializing a PI, it's simply concatenating the data without further escaping.\n\nUsing the escaping rules for XML attribute values (adding \\r\\n\\t) would enable XML roundtripping when using the intended API, and we could say that's an improvement and just do that.\n\nIf we also wanted to ensure that the attribute map as updated after setting `pi.data` survives roundtripping, then we'd need to normalize `pi.data` at some point, but that has high compat risk for uses of PIs that don't look like XML attributes.",
    "author_association": "MEMBER",
    "pin": null,
    "reactions": {
      "url": "https://api.github.com/repos/whatwg/dom/issues/comments/6823287865/reactions",
