    "created_at": "2026-11-12T16:55:15Z",
    "updated_at": "2026-11-12T16:55:15Z",
    "body": "I think that if we did want to replace U+000D, we should do it by also escaping U+0009 and U+000A, to match XML attribute escaping. Not because U+0009 and U+000A are problematic, but because it's simpler in implementation, you can just reuse an existing code path.\n\nHowever, since I don't think we can solve the problem with `pi.data`, I'll close this. Now the reasoning is documented if someone comes searching for it.",
